  "about": "The checklist reminder at the end of a turn: the executor's hook (internal/hook) runs these cases. A case plays its stops in order against one state and config directory. The claude running the hook is the process claude, its parent init, below it a shell, the hook's parent; claude keeps sessions/<pid>.json of itself in the config directory: pid, sessionId, cwd, procStart, kind interactive and name, its process started at start, with args from args by name or as given. A claude of a case lays its fields over these, null name for none, and over over the file. A checklist of a stop is written before it, under the place and name it names, with its file written at began plus written seconds (-60 when not given); over is laid over its file. A stop runs on the payload of a Stop of session with the transcript named, its payload laid over and drop taken out, or on input as it is; a transcript of null is a path to nothing. tail is how much of the transcript is read. holds says whether the stop is held with reason. names are the files of checklists the executor computes, sessionNames the name of a session from its file and its arguments, stamps the times of records in seconds, null for none.",
